  <content>
  <section><para dir="ltr">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="e33d6517-71c2-4b13-a3ad-973e596b0bce"><problem><para>
      <para>1. Chloe creates a scatter plot showing the relationship between the number of steps she takes and her heart rate. The correlation coefficient of the line of best fit is 0.88. </para>
      <para>Are they correlated? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
    </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>Yes, the correlation coefficient is close to 1, so they are correlated.</para><para>No, the correlation coefficient is close to 1.</para><para>Yes, the correlation coefficient is more than 0.</para><para>No, the correlation coefficient is more than 0.</para></problem><solution><para>Yes, the correlation coefficient is close to 1, so they are correlated.</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is: Yes, the correlation coefficient is close to 1, so they are correlated.

      </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
